      {
        "id": 153511,
        "name": "Sonvar",
        "username": "Powerhound_2000",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/{size}/1859_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-01-18T18:23:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Fynikz\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/f/9e8a1a/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Fynikz:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;Or is it just that his flechettes and technological superiority cards can inflict lots of board-clearance and damage and sometimes those result in things going south for the heros?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That would be part of it along with a bad timed Terraforming. &nbsp;Also games where you either don't have Ongoing destruction to get rid of Adaptive Plating Subroutine which slows the game down in Omnitron's favor if you have a smaller group. &nbsp; Omnitron can be a pushover at times but there are games I've been hammered by him. &nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Edit: &nbsp;Early EPEs can be deadly too when you aren't setup to deal with it yet. &nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:32:51.753Z",
