      {
        "id": 153512,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-01-18T18:26:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Fynikz\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/f/9e8a1a/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Fynikz:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Or is it just that his flechettes and technological superiority cards can inflict lots of board-clearance and damage and sometimes those result in things going south for the heros?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>This. Plus very bad timed 15-damage-a-pop bombs. I guess you have never seen a bomb come out at the worst time when theres nothing you can do about it. If so you are far luckier than most and I'd consider you a major statistical outlier.</p>\n<p>Try playing him on advanced (something I recomend with all of the \"easy\" villains). In addition, Omnitron II is a tougher variation you might find more pleasing.</p>",
