      {
        "id": 153514,
        "name": "Fynikz",
        "username": "Fynikz",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/f/9e8a1a/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2016-01-18T19:52:38.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Fynikz wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Or is it just that his flechettes and technological superiority cards can inflict lots of board-clearance and damage and sometimes those result in things going south for the heros?\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nThis. Plus very bad timed 15-damage-a-pop bombs. I guess you have never seen a bomb come out at the worst time when theres nothing you can do about it. If so you are far luckier than most and I'd consider you a major statistical outlier.Try playing him on advanced (something I recomend with all of the \"easy\" villains). In addition, Omnitron II is a tougher variation you might find more pleasing.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I almost forgot those bombs existed. We've seen them, but it seems like every time they come up we've got something that can deal with them in an inappropriately easy way (Nightmist or Tachyon redirecting their damage back at them, Visionary using Wrest the Mind, etc.). I could definitely see the game being hard if in his play-2-villain-cards mode or via Terraforming he throws out a board wipe followed by a bomb.</p>\n<p>Thanks for clearing that up. It's good to know we're playing it correctly, we've just been fortunate not to ever have his wombo-combos come out on us.</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:32:52.013Z",
